From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:46:57 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the SHA-3 instructions

EOR3, BCAX, RAX1 and XAR (FEAT_SHA3) are available as intrinsics. They
compute the column parities, the theta and rho rotations and the chi step
of Keccak-f[1600] on two lanes per register. The rotation of XAR is an
immediate in [0, 63].

armv8a_simd_facts.v states that XAR by 64 - r rotates each lane left by
r, the rotation of rho.
